;; Package emu is the frame of Arbace's machine emulators (doc/asm/AMD64.md §10; AX5-DESIGN §1, AXS52 (a)): a Linux
;; process's address space over crt's Mem (crt's slabs hold the bytes; emu keeps the permissions per page, Linux's layout and
;; a software TLB), its loader (a static ELF executable and the stack Linux builds for it) and the part of the kernel a
;; machine needs beyond crt's system calls (brk, mmap, munmap, mprotect). It imports std and arbace/crt only.
